.TH CHECK-AI-IMAGES 1 "2026-08-07" "check-ai-images" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
check-ai-images \- scan subdirectories for AI-generation image metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B check-ai-images
[\fB\-v\fP]
[\fIdirectory\fP]
.br
.B check-ai-images
[\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B check-ai-images
inspects the image files inside the immediate subdirectories of the target
directory and reports which subdirectories contain images carrying
AI-generation metadata, using
.BR exiftool (1).
.P
For each immediate subdirectory (depth 1, not recursive), a sample of at most
.B 3
images is taken (jpg, jpeg, png, webp, avif, heic, heif, tiff, tif, bmp, gif,
jxl). Each sample is dumped as JSON with
.B exiftool \-j
and every metadata value is matched, case-insensitively, against the detection
patterns listed in DETECTION PATTERNS. A single match flags the whole
subdirectory.
.P
A final summary is printed:
.IP \(bu 2
directories containing AI metadata, prefixed
.B [AI]
.IP \(bu 2
directories with no AI metadata, prefixed
.B [--]
.IP \(bu 2
directories containing no supported image files, prefixed
.B [??]
(only shown if any)
.P
In verbose mode, the matching file and pattern are also reported to standard
error for each flagged directory, as the scan runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose. For each flagged directory, print the triggering file and matched
pattern to standard error:
.RS
.PD 0
.TP
[AI]
\fIdirectory\fP
.TP
file:
\fIfilename\fP
.TP
match:
\fIpattern label\fP
.PD
.RE
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print the usage summary and exit with status 1.
.TP
.I directory
Target directory to scan. Defaults to the current working directory. Must be
a directory; otherwise an error is printed and the script exits with status 1.
.SH DETECTION PATTERNS
An image is flagged if any of its metadata values matches one of the
following signatures:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Tool signatures
(substring match): Midjourney, Stable Diffusion, DALL\-E (also DALL\(pcE),
NovelAI, Leonardo AI, Adobe Firefly, Bing Image Creator, ComfyUI,
Automatic1111, InvokeAI, CivitAI, DreamStudio, craiyon, Artbreeder, Wombo,
DeepAI, NightCafe, Playground (Playground AI), Ideogram, Flux, SDXL, A1111,
DiffusionBee, Fooocus, RuDALL\-E, Kandinsky, SwarmUI, tidybot, StableSwarmUI,
Promptrr, PromptsPal, StylePrompt.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Generic AI labels:
AI\-generated, generated by AI, generated with AI, synthetic, AITag,
AIMetadata, AI_Generated.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Stable Diffusion PNG Parameters:
a
.I Parameters
tag whose value contains "negative prompt", "Negative prompt", "Steps:",
"Sampler:", "CFG scale", "Seed:", or "Model hash".
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan the current directory:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images
.EE
.P
Scan a specific tree:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images ~/Pictures
.EE
.P
Show which file and pattern triggered each detection:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images \-v ~/Downloads
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed.
.TP
.B 1
Help was shown, an unknown option was given, or the target is not a
directory.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B exiftool
must be installed (from
.BR perl-image-exiftool ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR exiftool (1),
.BR find (1)
